  "text": "Ester Yang, DVM, DACVIM | Veterinary Oncology — DVM STAT Consulting\n0\nSkip to Content\nTeleconsultations\nSpecialists\nTestimonials\nAbout\nHow it Works\nCE Hub\nBlog\nCareers\nClinic Login\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nTeleconsultations\nSpecialists\nTestimonials\nAbout\nHow it Works\nCE Hub\nBlog\nCareers\nClinic Login\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nTeleconsultations\nSpecialists\nTestimonials\nAbout\nHow it Works\nCE Hub\nBlog\nCareers\nClinic Login\nEster Yang, VMD, MS, DACVIM (Oncology)\nDr. Ester Yang grew up in the DC area and received her veterinary degree from the University of Pennsylvania. She completed a small animal medicine and surgery internship at Angell Animal Medical Center in Boston. Dr. Yang earned her Master of Science degree and completed a medical oncology residency at Virginia-Maryland College of Veterinary Medicine in 2023. She serves as an assistant professor at the University of Pennsylvania. Dr. Yang is passionate about bridging the gap in making medical oncology care accessible for providers not close to a specialty clinic.\nThrough 24/7 Board-Certified Specialist Teleconsultation, we\nbridge the gap to specialty care\nfor veterinarians in general, emergency, and mobile practices, empowering vets with access to specialist guidance.\nFAQ\nDVM STAT is a\nproud VHMA Sponsor\n, supporting veterinary managers and teams in delivering accessible, collaborative specialty care\nPhone Consult STAT Line:\n833-386-7828\ninfo@dvmstat.com\nCreate Free Account\nFor Practice Owners\nLeave a Testimonial\nClinic Login\n©Copyright 2026 DVM STAT® Consulting. All rights reserved. No portion of this site may be reproduced without permission.\nTerms and Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility",
